# 🔒 Gitleaks: Shift-Left Secrets Detection Pipeline

> Detect and block hardcoded secrets (AWS keys, GitHub tokens, API keys, database passwords) before they reach production using Gitleaks, GitHub Actions, and pre-commit hooks.

📊 *84% of security breaches involve exposed credentials (Verizon DBIR)*

---

## 🎯 Problem Statement

Developers often accidentally commit sensitive information such as API keys, database passwords, and cloud credentials into source code. Once pushed to Git, these secrets can remain in history permanently, even if deleted.

This project solves that problem by implementing a shift-left security approach that detects and blocks secrets early in the development lifecycle.

---

## 🛡️ Solution Overview (3-Layer Defense)

This system enforces security at multiple stages:

- Pre-commit Hook → Blocks secrets before commit
- GitHub Actions CI/CD → Fails pipeline if secrets are detected
- Git History Scan → Detects secrets in full commit history

---

## ⚙️ Architecture

Developer → Pre-commit Hook → GitHub Actions → GitHub Security Dashboard

Each layer runs Gitleaks to ensure no secrets reach production.

---

## 🚀 Quick Start

Clone the repository and set up the environment:

git clone https://github.com/YOURUSERNAME/gitleaks-demo
cd gitleaks-demo

Install Gitleaks:
brew install gitleaks

Install pre-commit:
pip install pre-commit
pre-commit install

---

## 🧪 Test the System

echo 'GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_fake123' > bad.py
git add bad.py
git commit -m "test secret detection"

The commit will be blocked automatically by the pre-commit hook.

