- GitHub Security tab displays detected findings via SARIF

---

## 🛠️ Pre-commit Configuration

repos:
  - repo: https://github.com/gitleaks/gitleaks
    rev: v8.18.4
    hooks:
      - id: gitleaks

---

## ⚙️ GitHub Actions Pipeline

name: Secret Scanning

on:
  push:
    branches: ["**"]
  pull_request:
    branches: [main]

jobs:
  scan:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest

    permissions:
      contents: read
      security-events: write

    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
        with:
          fetch-depth: 0

      - name: Install Gitleaks
        run: |
          curl -sSL https://github.com/gitleaks/gitleaks/releases/download/v8.18.4/gitleaks_8.18.4_linux_x64.tar.gz | tar -xz
          sudo mv gitleaks /usr/local/bin/

      - name: Run Gitleaks
        run: |
          gitleaks detect --source . --report-format sarif --report-path results.sarif --exit-code 1

      - name: Upload SARIF
        if: always()
        uses: github/codeql-action/upload-sarif@v3
        with:
          sarif_file: results.sarif

---

## 🔍 How Gitleaks Works

- Regex Engine → Detects known patterns like AWS, GitHub, Stripe keys
- Entropy Analysis → Detects high-randomness secret-like strings
- Git History Scan → Scans all commits, not just current files
- SARIF Output → Integrates with GitHub Security dashboard

